---
// Melbourne's Make Good Specialists section
---

<section class="mg-specialists">
  <div class="mg-specialists__inner">
    <h2 class="mg-specialists__heading">Commercial Make Good Specialists<br /><span class="mg-specialists__accent">Melbourne</span></h2>
    <div class="mg-specialists__copy">
      We work with tenants, property managers and owners to restore commercial spaces to their original condition. One contractor. One quote. Every trade covered.
    </div>
    <div class="mg-specialists__body">
      <p>
        A make good is the work a tenant must complete at lease end to return a space to the condition set out in the lease. For offices that usually means removing partitions and fitout, capping services, and repairing floors, walls and ceilings. For warehouses it often means racking removal, floor restoration and line marking.
      </p>
      <p>
        We inspect the site, review your lease obligations and give you a fixed price quote that covers every trade. A small office strip out can take 1 to 2 weeks and a large warehouse restoration 4 to 8 weeks, so the earlier you call, the easier it is to meet your handover date. Beyond lease end, we also deliver <a href="/services/remediation-solutions/">building remediation</a> and <a href="/services/roofing-solutions/">commercial roofing</a>. New to the process? Read our <a href="/learn/make-good-guide/">make good guide</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Remediation Micro-Callout -->
    <div class="mg-specialists__micro-callout">
      <h3 class="mg-specialists__micro-heading">Structural issues don't wait.</h3>
      <p class="mg-specialists__micro-body">
        Building problems need engineered solutions. Concrete cancer, water ingress, cladding compliance—we diagnose the cause and deliver certified repairs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .mg-specialists {
    padding: 56px 24px 58px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .mg-specialists__inner {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .mg-specialists__heading {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.25;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: #ffffff;
  }
  .mg-specialists__accent {
    color: #F28C3A;
  }
  .mg-specialists__copy {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    margin: 0 0 32px;
  }
  
  .mg-specialists__body {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto 32px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .mg-specialists__body p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .mg-specialists__body a {
    color: #F28C3A;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  /* Remediation Micro-Callout */
  .mg-specialists__micro-callout {
    margin: 24px auto 0;
    max-width: 680px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .mg-specialists__micro-heading {
    font-size: clamp(22px, 2.5vw, 28px);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #ffffff;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .mg-specialists__micro-body {
    font-size: 18px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.75);
    margin: 0;
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .mg-specialists {
      padding: 64px 16px 40px;
    }
    .mg-specialists__copy {
      font-size: 16px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    .mg-specialists__micro-callout {
      margin: 20px auto 0;
    }
    .mg-specialists__micro-heading {
      font-size: 22px;
    }
    .mg-specialists__micro-body {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
